// Decision D37 -- strict-typing ratchet. The include list only grows:
// add a module once it passes strict, never remove one. The disabled
// reportUnknown* family measures numpy's incomplete stubs, not our API
// contracts.
//
// All of src/comnumpy is on this list as of the py.typed commit, so the
// gate the architecture document set -- no partial py.typed, since one
// is worse than none -- is met and src/comnumpy/py.typed ships. The list
// is now a *completeness* check as much as a ratchet: a new module that
// is not added here is a module whose types the marker file promises and
// nothing verifies.
